From: Uke Linux contributors <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: preserve Uke missing-graph unmap refusal on 7.3.4

Linux7.3.4 already carries the map-type token, returned status and selected
handle fix. Keep its apm-based unmap helper, removal-time mapping cleanup,
position reset and error logging. Retain the cumulative Uke refusal to alter
the shared response or wake a waiter for an absent graph.

Signed-off-by: Uke Linux contributors <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm.c
@@ -1038,8 +1038,6 @@
 			wake_up(&apm->wait);
 			break;
 		case APM_CMD_SHARED_MEM_UNMAP_REGIONS:
-			apm->result.opcode = result->opcode;
-			apm->result.status = result->status;
 			if (result->status)
 				dev_err(dev, "Error (%d) Processing 0x%08x cmd\n", result->status,
 					result->opcode);
@@ -1048,13 +1046,16 @@
 			is_pos_buf = hdr->token & APM_MMAP_TOKEN_MAP_TYPE_POS_BUF;
 
 			info = idr_find(&apm->graph_info_idr, graph_id);
-			if (info && !result->status) {
+			if (!info)
+				break;
+			if (!result->status) {
 				if (is_pos_buf)
 					info->pos_buf_mem_map_handle = 0;
 				else
 					info->mem_map_handle = 0;
 			}
 
+			apm->result = *result;
 			wake_up(&apm->wait);
 			break;
 		default:
